\newlabel{fig:crosssuite}{{9}{19}{$\pi _{0.5}$ cross-suite pruning profiles. Object random (green solid) exhibits a deep cliff at $k \in [0.85, 0.925]$ with 68\,pp recovery, absent on Spatial (blue solid). L2 norm (dashed) maintains a plateau on both suites through the cliff zone}{figure.caption.45}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces $\pi _{0.5}$ token importance spatial distribution (16$\times $16 grid, averaged over timesteps). Left: LIBERO-Object shows a pronounced center-high, edge-low pattern (center rows 7--9: norm $\sim $265--267; edge rows 0, 14--15: norm $\sim $235--236; CV${=}$0.066). Right: LIBERO-Spatial exhibits a flatter distribution (center-edge gap 14.67 vs.\ 21.87; CV${=}$0.059). The 33\% center-edge gap difference quantitatively explains Object's sharp cliff versus Spatial's graceful degradation under random removal.}}{20}{figure.caption.46}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:token_heatmap}{{10}{20}{$\pi _{0.5}$ token importance spatial distribution (16$\times $16 grid, averaged over timesteps). Left: LIBERO-Object shows a pronounced center-high, edge-low pattern (center rows 7--9: norm $\sim $265--267; edge rows 0, 14--15: norm $\sim $235--236; CV${=}$0.066). Right: LIBERO-Spatial exhibits a flatter distribution (center-edge gap 14.67 vs.\ 21.87; CV${=}$0.059). The 33\% center-edge gap difference quantitatively explains Object's sharp cliff versus Spatial's graceful degradation under random removal}{figure.caption.46}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Hypergeometric cliff model for $\pi _{0.5}$ Object random pruning. (a)~Model-predicted collapse probability (dashed) vs.\ observed success rate (solid) across the cliff zone $k \in [0.85, 0.95]$; RMSE${=}$0.018. (b)~$P(\text  {collapse})$ curves for Object ($C{=}106$, concentrated) and Spatial ($C \approx 5$, distributed), illustrating why Object exhibits a sharp phase transition absent on Spatial.}}{20}{figure.caption.47}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cliff_model}{{11}{20}{Hypergeometric cliff model for $\pi _{0.5}$ Object random pruning. (a)~Model-predicted collapse probability (dashed) vs.\ observed success rate (solid) across the cliff zone $k \in [0.85, 0.95]$; RMSE${=}$0.018. (b)~$P(\text {collapse})$ curves for Object ($C{=}106$, concentrated) and Spatial ($C \approx 5$, distributed), illustrating why Object exhibits a sharp phase transition absent on Spatial}{figure.caption.47}{}}
